  "claim": "Munich beat the Tajikistan in a sporting event. Jack Taylor (referee) was famous for officiating at this event.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Football in Munich. Sentence: Munich is one of the most successful footballing cities in Europe and the World with over 40 trophies, including Germany's victory in the 1974 FIFA World Cup Final.\nPage: 1974 FIFA World Cup Final. Sentence: The 1974 FIFA World Cup Final was the final match of the 1974 FIFA World Cup, the 10th FIFA World Cup, a competition to determine the world champion among national men's football sides.\nPage: 1974 FIFA World Cup Final. Sentence: The match was contested by the Netherlands and West Germany, with the West Germans winning 2–1.\nPage: Jack Taylor (referee). Sentence: John Keith \"Jack\" Taylor, OBE (21 April 1930 – 27 July 2012) was an English football referee, famous for officiating in the 1974 FIFA World Cup Final during which he awarded two penalties in the first 30 minutes.",
