        "original_id": "cd3e9bbb-a117-5c3f-a1d9-0b8f5bf63e49",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Munich\n- Events: 1974 FIFA World Cup Final, 1974 FIFA World Cup\n- Teams: West Germany, Netherlands\n- People: Jack Taylor\n- Roles: football referee\n- Topics: football success, world championship\n\nFacts:\n- The 1974 FIFA World Cup was the 10th FIFA World Cup and was a competition to determine the world champion among national men's football sides.\n- The 1974 FIFA World Cup Final was the final match of the 1974 FIFA World Cup.\n- The 1974 FIFA World Cup Final was contested by the Netherlands and West Germany, and West Germany won 2–1.\n- Jack Taylor was an English football referee who officiated the 1974 FIFA World Cup Final and awarded two penalties in the first 30 minutes.\n- Munich is described as one of the most successful footballing cities in Europe and the world, with over 40 trophies, including Germany's victory in the 1974 FIFA World Cup Final.",
